WEBVTT

00:03.380 --> 00:07.090
<i>Nii-chan, thank you for the souvenirs from Hokkaido!</i>

00:07.480 --> 00:09.010
<i>You're just so cool!</i>

00:09.170 --> 00:11.870
<i>You always buy me things that I've wanted!</i>

00:12.410 --> 00:14.310
<i>But you know, I...</i>

00:14.500 --> 00:17.540
10
salted
salmon

00:15.620 --> 00:16.840
<i>...don't need this much.</i>

00:18.690 --> 00:19.940
Amazing!

00:20.360 --> 00:22.180
I have a bear wood carving,

00:22.470 --> 00:24.940
but it's the first time I've seen one catching 3 salmons!

00:25.670 --> 00:28.380
Takahiro's choice of these things is really something.

00:29.180 --> 00:33.330
<i>Rather... 3 bear wood carvings are not required!</i>

00:33.620 --> 00:35.820
What is nii-chan thinking!?

00:35.920 --> 00:37.340
Honestly!

00:37.600 --> 00:41.400
Oh, speaking of bears, Usagi-san, please do something about the bear room!

00:41.810 --> 00:46.510
Just the other day, I got caught up in a bear avalanche!

00:47.660 --> 00:50.300
The overflowing bears can just go in the back room then.

00:50.640 --> 00:55.960
A certain someone's 1/24th scale model of the Great Wall is twisting and turning all over the floor over there!

00:56.220 --> 00:57.450
Then in the next room?

00:57.600 --> 01:00.050
Your model train set is choo-chooing around over there!

01:00.440 --> 01:01.370
Then the neighbouring room?

01:01.370 --> 01:03.140
Marimo are growing there!

01:03.950 --> 01:04.640
Hmm...

01:05.420 --> 01:07.190
I'll buy another mansion.

01:06.350 --> 01:08.920
Save the money for your old age!

01:09.780 --> 01:13.000
<i>Honestly... all because he's the little rich lord.</i>

01:14.370 --> 01:16.230
<i>But, I'm a bit relieved.</i>

01:16.900 --> 01:18.600
<i>He's the usual Usagi-san.</i>

01:19.400 --> 01:23.500
<i>Lately, he's been acting a bit weird, so I was worried.</i>

01:25.490 --> 01:26.720
What's for breakfast today?

01:27.060 --> 01:28.880
Salmon and komatsuna marinade,

01:28.940 --> 01:32.740
miso soup with salmon, salmon with rice, salmon butter saute.

01:32.880 --> 01:34.680
The saute's for lunch, so just reheat it.

01:35.380 --> 01:36.740
It's going to be salmon for a while.

01:37.120 --> 01:38.920
I like salmon, so it's fine.

01:39.320 --> 01:42.450
Also, we've already got many bear wood carvings,

01:42.820 --> 01:45.960
so is it okay if we keep just one of Nii-chan's souvenir and give out the rest?

01:46.320 --> 01:46.860
Yeah.

01:47.360 --> 01:50.750
I'm already giving Sumi-senpai some salmon, so maybe I could also give him one of the carvings too.

01:52.630 --> 01:54.960
Oh, by the way, Usagi-san, I...

01:54.980 --> 01:56.760
Hey, wa-wai-wait! Usagi-san!

01:56.840 --> 01:59.400
The stove's on! That's danger-

01:59.500 --> 02:00.110
Ah! Wai-!

02:01.980 --> 02:03.140
Stop it!!

02:06.420 --> 02:07.250
Misaki...

02:09.570 --> 02:10.400
I...

02:16.940 --> 02:19.660
Oh no! The miso soup's boiling over!

02:20.740 --> 02:22.860
Whoa! Look at the time!

02:23.710 --> 02:24.630
I'm leaving!

02:24.660 --> 02:27.320
I have a night shift at work today, so I'll be a little late!

02:28.330 --> 02:31.220
Oh, that's right! I wrapped the saute in aluminium foil,

02:31.300 --> 02:32.950
so make sure to take it off before reheating,

02:33.010 --> 02:34.640
or there will be a disaster in the microwave!

02:35.280 --> 02:36.090
Misaki.

02:36.710 --> 02:38.940
How about you start thinking of living alone from now on?

02:44.020 --> 02:49.020
Moon in the clouds, flower in the wind

02:49.330 --> 02:54.580
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

02:49.330 --> 02:54.580
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

02:52.760 --> 03:06.030
Junjou Romantica 2

02:54.580 --> 02:58.050
ima futari no story

02:54.580 --> 02:58.050
Now, our story...

02:59.340 --> 03:06.830
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

02:59.340 --> 03:06.830
Our future is going to shine on.

03:10.270 --> 03:15.560
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

03:10.270 --> 03:15.560
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

03:16.030 --> 03:20.390
okubyou ni naru bakari

03:16.030 --> 03:20.390
and always lose my nerve.

03:20.390 --> 03:25.990
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

03:20.390 --> 03:25.990
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

03:25.990 --> 03:29.620
kimi to aeru nara

03:25.990 --> 03:29.620
if it means I can see you.

03:31.650 --> 03:36.630
ame ni utarete furueru koe

03:31.650 --> 03:36.630
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

03:36.960 --> 03:42.230
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

03:36.960 --> 03:42.230
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

03:42.910 --> 03:45.710
boku wa yuku yo

03:42.910 --> 03:45.710
I'll go,

03:45.710 --> 03:52.460
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

03:45.710 --> 03:52.460
Until the day when I can see you.

03:53.280 --> 03:58.470
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

03:53.280 --> 03:58.470
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

03:58.470 --> 04:02.180
ima futari no story

03:58.470 --> 04:02.180
Now, our story

04:02.340 --> 04:03.990
ugokidashita

04:02.340 --> 04:03.990
has started.

04:03.990 --> 04:08.980
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

04:03.990 --> 04:08.980
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

04:08.980 --> 04:16.170
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

04:08.980 --> 04:16.170
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

04:22.260 --> 04:24.540
Eh... Wha... Oh!

04:24.900 --> 04:26.320
Yeah, right, right.

04:26.750 --> 04:28.710
Nii-chan said something to you, didn't he?

04:28.960 --> 04:32.460
Man, he's just too overprotective, so don't bother about it much.

04:33.070 --> 04:33.840
No.

04:41.950 --> 04:42.910
<i>It's strange.</i>

04:43.320 --> 04:45.360
<i>Usagi-san's definitely acting weird.</i>

04:45.960 --> 04:49.620
Oh crap! I'm gonna be so late! Anyway see you later!

04:51.780 --> 04:53.720
<i>What is it? What's going on?</i>

04:53.720 --> 04:56.560
<i>Why would he tell me to live on my own?</i>

04:56.780 --> 04:59.680
<i>The usual Usagi-san would never say something like that.</i>

04:59.860 --> 05:01.310
<i>Is he bogged down with work?</i>

05:01.450 --> 05:03.820
<i>No, he finished a big job just recently.</i>

05:06.820 --> 05:11.890
<i>Now that I think about it, these days, he doesn't say "I love you" like he always used to.</i>

05:12.600 --> 05:15.810
<i>That said, he might just be acting like this on a whim.</i>

05:16.540 --> 05:21.170
<i>No, even if he's doing this on a whim, he isn't the sort of person to do that.</i>

05:22.700 --> 05:26.150
<i>What to do!? I feel so shaken up right now.</i>

05:28.290 --> 05:29.000
Don't want it.

05:29.650 --> 05:33.710
Don't say that! Look! There's 3 salmons!

05:34.020 --> 05:36.520
And this elegant design, bursting with such energy and life!

05:36.720 --> 05:40.440
You see, I prefer my wooden bear carvings with only bear in it.

05:40.770 --> 05:41.990
No way...

05:42.090 --> 05:44.650
Your ridiculously specific taste is so weird.

05:44.900 --> 05:47.560
Like when you said you didn't like how big the cherry pits are.

05:47.780 --> 05:51.030
By the way, the size of the loquat seeds is criminally large.

05:49.380 --> 05:54.690
The loquat seed: So huge it's like,
"Are you <i>trying</i> to stop me from eating you?"

05:51.260 --> 05:54.520
Yeah, they certainly underestimate a person.

05:56.770 --> 05:58.920
By the way, is Usagi-san well?

06:01.420 --> 06:02.700
Why do you ask?

06:02.980 --> 06:05.960
Nah, I was just wondering if he was doing well or not.

06:06.640 --> 06:07.560
Did something happen?

06:08.560 --> 06:12.160
I still don't get what you are thinking,

06:12.480 --> 06:15.040
or understand just how much of it is true or false.

06:15.470 --> 06:18.120
What's with that? I'm always truthful you know.

06:18.640 --> 06:23.520
Besides, a certain someone insisting on being so evasive encouraged me to make a move.

06:24.020 --> 06:24.750
Eh?

06:25.620 --> 06:26.350
What?

06:27.450 --> 06:28.660
Did I say something?

06:31.700 --> 06:33.190
<i>I'm evasive?</i>

06:33.740 --> 06:35.150
<i>That's not true.</i>

06:36.250 --> 06:38.310
<i>I always make myself clear to everyone, no matter how many times.</i>

06:41.340 --> 06:46.100
<i>Anyway, what Usagi-san told me this morning is still weighing on my mind.</i>

06:48.380 --> 06:50.320
Misaki... I...

06:54.380 --> 06:57.350
<i>What was he about to say at that time?</i>

07:05.250 --> 07:07.520
<i>It's crowded! Buy your tickets already!</i>

07:09.090 --> 07:09.580
<i>Huh?</i>

07:11.270 --> 07:12.090
Excuse me...

07:13.380 --> 07:15.470
If it's okay, I can check the cost.

07:15.740 --> 07:16.260
Eh?

07:16.620 --> 07:18.440
Ahh... I mean on the route map.

07:19.510 --> 07:21.020
No, I can see that.

07:21.880 --> 07:23.940
I wanted to go to Teito Hotel.

07:24.620 --> 07:26.820
Then it's 260 yen.

07:26.860 --> 07:28.700
I see. Thank you.

07:33.600 --> 07:35.160
<i>This person, could it be...</i>

07:36.260 --> 07:38.180
<i>...he hasn't been on a train before?</i>

07:39.620 --> 07:40.420
Excuse me...

07:42.110 --> 07:44.820
I'm getting off for my job at the stop before.

07:45.160 --> 07:46.780
If it's okay, would you like to go together?

07:52.570 --> 07:54.840
What's with this scenerio?

07:55.720 --> 07:58.660
Haven't I done this once before?

08:02.380 --> 08:06.480
<i>And I have a vague recollection that </i>that<i> was the prologue to a very unfortunate incident...</i>

08:07.420 --> 08:11.000
I'm sorry for troubling you with this.

08:11.250 --> 08:12.830
Oh, no no.

08:13.120 --> 08:15.890
I think it's been about 20 years since I rode on a train.

08:16.040 --> 08:17.060
20 years!?

08:17.400 --> 08:19.600
The world sure has become a more convenient place.

08:19.880 --> 08:22.480
Thanks to your kindness I was really saved.

08:23.960 --> 08:28.370
Everyone else whom I asked either said something to get rid of me or ignored me.

08:29.600 --> 08:35.650
<i>Well, a dude dressed in all black with sunglasses on a weekday evening is the definition of a suspicious character.</i>

08:29.600 --> 08:32.320
Gloves

08:29.600 --> 08:35.730
Black head-to-toe

08:31.810 --> 08:35.720
Sunglasses

08:35.320 --> 08:35.720
Weekday evening

08:35.320 --> 08:35.720
Tall

08:37.920 --> 08:38.760
Oops.

08:39.030 --> 08:39.970
Sorry.

08:40.420 --> 08:41.490
Ohh!!

08:42.640 --> 08:44.230
This is wonderful!

08:44.310 --> 08:44.800
Eh?

08:46.080 --> 08:48.370
I have a wood carving of a bear myself,

08:48.460 --> 08:51.560
but this is the first time I'm seeing one catching 3 salmons!

08:52.040 --> 08:54.750
May I ask from where did you buy this?

08:55.020 --> 08:57.380
Oh, this is a souvenir from Hokkaido.

08:57.520 --> 08:59.000
If you like it, you can keep it.

08:59.490 --> 09:01.310
We have 2 more just like this one.

09:01.640 --> 09:03.460
Eh? But...

09:03.530 --> 09:06.720
Ah, please, I insist! It's an extra, so don't worry about it.

09:07.060 --> 09:08.000
Lucky!

09:08.560 --> 09:09.750
Excuse me.

09:10.080 --> 09:13.470
I certainly wasn't expecting to receive something so nice in a place like this.

09:14.560 --> 09:17.660
Well then, I too had a little something extra leftover...

09:18.010 --> 09:20.280
Would you accept it in return?

09:21.600 --> 09:22.570
A duck?

09:22.780 --> 09:24.930
I just bought too many of them.

09:25.530 --> 09:31.960
You see, I have a son, and I was thinking of using these to liven up our bath time together.

09:32.580 --> 09:34.020
With your son?

09:34.760 --> 09:39.120
I'm sure this is quiet common, our relationship isn't so good.

09:39.360 --> 09:44.790
I thought that maybe if we talked to each other while bathing, we'd open up to each other in some way.

09:45.760 --> 09:46.710
I see.

09:47.280 --> 09:49.620
How old is your son?

09:50.320 --> 09:52.400
31, I think.

09:52.560 --> 09:54.450
<i>31 !!!</i>

09:55.190 --> 09:55.950
<i>He's weird.</i>

09:56.050 --> 09:57.660
<i>This person definitely is weird.</i>

09:58.620 --> 10:04.640
How to say this, I guess you have to make sure you put things into words when necessary.

10:06.170 --> 10:09.040
No matter how strongly you feel in your heart,

10:09.550 --> 10:12.900
if you don't convey it to the other person, it's meaningless.

10:14.360 --> 10:16.350
It's quiet difficult to do.

10:27.970 --> 10:30.070
Oh, your stop is the next one.

10:30.200 --> 10:32.300
Oh no, I'll stop here as well.

10:32.650 --> 10:35.480
Could I treat you to some tea as thanks for the bear?

10:35.890 --> 10:37.980
Oh no, the sentiment itself is enough.

10:38.590 --> 10:40.760
Oh, excuse me.

10:42.700 --> 10:43.400
It's me.

10:44.950 --> 10:46.160
Okay, I understand.

10:46.670 --> 10:47.580
Sorry.

10:48.040 --> 10:52.160
It's a shame since I invited you for tea just now, but they've found out where I am.

10:52.490 --> 10:54.610
Seems like a car's waiting for me at the exit.

10:55.000 --> 10:56.730
Oh, no no! No problem at all.

10:59.340 --> 11:01.430
I'm glad that I met you today.

11:01.720 --> 11:05.480
I must say, the idea of getting on a train after 20 years was a little daunting.

11:06.360 --> 11:07.640
It was fun.

11:08.030 --> 11:11.160
Oh, it's good if you are happy.

11:13.450 --> 11:16.180
Ah, but why did you feel like riding one today?

11:16.460 --> 11:18.120
Um, actually...

11:18.230 --> 11:19.080
President.

11:21.220 --> 11:22.650
I've been looking for you.

11:22.970 --> 11:24.480
<i>Elder Usagi!!!</i>

11:25.680 --> 11:27.360
Why are you with him?

11:27.560 --> 11:29.360
Err... n-no reason...!

11:29.460 --> 11:32.190
He taught me how to ride on the train.

11:32.310 --> 11:35.200
I heard from my secretary that you'd ridden on it once before.

11:35.940 --> 11:37.500
I was wondering what it was like.

11:37.500 --> 11:41.040
Ahh... um... so you're the president of a company?

11:41.690 --> 11:42.640
He's my father.

11:42.980 --> 11:45.890
<i>Usagi's father!!!</i>

11:56.710 --> 11:59.040
Um, thank you very much for the cherries!

11:59.260 --> 12:01.440
Just, seriously, I truly don't want any more!

12:01.740 --> 12:02.400
Bye!

12:02.740 --> 12:03.900
Hey, you!

12:05.990 --> 12:07.160
Your acquaintance?

12:08.100 --> 12:09.140
Akihiko's.

12:15.510 --> 12:18.170
<i>Nii-chan, nii-chan! I'm scared!!</i>

12:18.230 --> 12:21.150
<i>Why did I have to met Usagi's father even!?</i>

12:22.760 --> 12:25.310
That's it, I'm (emitting) Usa-mones...

12:29.520 --> 12:32.560
Do Usa-mones... only work on men?

12:37.040 --> 12:38.320
<i>Just what is going on!?</i>

12:38.540 --> 12:43.200
<i>Ever since I met Usagi-san, I've been running into all kinds of crazy situations.</i>

12:44.020 --> 12:45.050
<i>Usagi-san...</i>

12:48.000 --> 12:50.710
<i>Why does Usagi-san not say anything clearly?</i>

12:52.490 --> 12:54.200
<i>All would be good if he just told me.</i>

12:55.530 --> 12:56.750
<i>Usagi-san...</i>

12:57.760 --> 13:00.190
<i>What is it that he wants me to do?</i>

13:02.050 --> 13:02.840
I'm back!

13:05.500 --> 13:06.480
What's wrong?

13:07.530 --> 13:08.470
Welcome back.

13:08.600 --> 13:11.240
When I was pouring coffee into the glass it just broke.

13:11.480 --> 13:13.020
What? You okay?

13:13.400 --> 13:13.950
I'm fine.

13:14.090 --> 13:15.800
Gah! You're bleeding!

13:16.010 --> 13:19.230
Sheesh! We have heat resistant glasses over here!

13:20.360 --> 13:21.620
Boring.

13:22.110 --> 13:22.820
What is?

13:23.300 --> 13:25.080
In the case of your finger bleeding,

13:25.400 --> 13:29.450
there's a rule saying that the other person has to suck on it to stop the bleeding,

13:29.740 --> 13:30.730
is what I saw on TV.

13:30.850 --> 13:32.770
There's no such rule.

13:34.040 --> 13:36.480
<i>Usagi-san's back to his usual self.</i>

13:37.050 --> 13:37.760
<i>But...</i>

13:38.240 --> 13:40.120
<i>...its no good leaving things just like this.</i>

13:40.700 --> 13:43.020
<i>I </i>must<i> properly set everything straight.</i>

13:43.660 --> 13:44.360
Got work?

13:44.830 --> 13:45.470
Yeah.

13:45.800 --> 13:47.470
Uh-Um, Usagi-san!

13:47.740 --> 13:48.390
What?

13:49.110 --> 13:51.760
Um, well, today at the station, I...

13:53.560 --> 13:54.440
<i>No.</i>

13:54.940 --> 13:58.720
<i>If I tell him about Usagi father, I'll have to talk about elder Usagi as well.</i>

14:00.760 --> 14:01.360
What is it?

14:01.690 --> 14:05.880
Ah, uh, no, I got 10 packs of pocket tissues at the station.

14:06.690 --> 14:07.490
Oh?

14:07.770 --> 14:09.120
You could blow your nose all day.

14:09.520 --> 14:11.080
Yeah, real hearty nose-blowing!

14:12.600 --> 14:13.190
What?

14:13.580 --> 14:17.870
Eh, uh..., oh no, I just thought I should change Suzuki-san's ribbon.

14:19.820 --> 14:20.440
Go ahead.

14:21.890 --> 14:22.620
Thank you.

14:28.830 --> 14:30.940
Sorry... even though you're busy...

14:31.320 --> 14:33.560
It's okay. It's just a simple column.

14:37.940 --> 14:41.600
<i>Really, the more I think, the less I understand.</i>

14:42.240 --> 14:44.810
<i>If he's got a problem with me, he should just tell me at once!</i>

14:45.960 --> 14:47.210
<i>Are the meals bad?</i>

14:47.800 --> 14:49.990
<i>But he eats everyday without leaving anything behind.</i>

14:50.880 --> 14:51.770
<i>Am I too noisy?</i>

14:52.410 --> 14:54.860
<i>But I don't yell unless he starts doing something weird.</i>

14:55.750 --> 14:56.760
<i>Am I in his way?</i>

14:57.470 --> 14:59.470
<i>But I am being careful that I remain silent.</i>

15:00.540 --> 15:03.040
Does he hate me now?

15:07.870 --> 15:09.200
U-Um...

15:10.000 --> 15:12.280
Do you have a problem with me?

15:12.810 --> 15:14.460
If you do, say it clearly!

15:15.890 --> 15:17.110
What's with this!?

15:17.240 --> 15:19.380
You've been acting weird since the other day!

15:20.320 --> 15:22.740
Is Sumi-senpai that much on your mind?

15:23.510 --> 15:24.480
Let me just say this,

15:24.760 --> 15:28.660
he's not a bad guy, but you never know just how serious he actually is!

15:29.030 --> 15:31.320
This morning, too,  you started saying weird things all of a sudden...

15:31.520 --> 15:32.560
What's up with that!?

15:32.960 --> 15:35.140
Even though you said you'd lock me up if I tried to run away,

15:35.290 --> 15:37.710
your actions and words are totally different!

15:38.480 --> 15:42.290
Actually, I would really appreciate it if you were just blunt with me!

15:42.560 --> 15:44.880
Like if I was getting in your way or being annoying.

15:45.320 --> 15:46.480
It's not like that.

15:46.960 --> 15:47.870
You too...

15:48.630 --> 15:52.360
What is it!? What did I do? I just don't get it!

15:55.340 --> 15:57.170
<i>Why is he not saying anything?</i>

15:57.690 --> 15:58.980
<i>What is on his mind?</i>

15:59.450 --> 16:01.590
<i>Then, does he want me to be the one to say it?</i>

16:05.190 --> 16:08.180
Do you hate me now?

16:08.990 --> 16:10.180
What <i>is</i> it!?

16:10.330 --> 16:12.240
Even though you keep blabbering unnecessary things,

16:12.400 --> 16:15.220
if you suddenly become silent, then I, too, would feel uneasy!

16:15.780 --> 16:18.920
Who's the one who kept on saying, "I love you, I love you" uselessly!?

16:20.070 --> 16:20.960
<i>That's right.</i>

16:21.210 --> 16:24.210
<i>And he used to call my name over and over so much that it was embarrassing too!</i>

16:25.010 --> 16:26.030
<i>Saying, "I love you"...</i>

16:27.020 --> 16:27.570
<i>Huh?</i>

16:28.520 --> 16:30.740
I... love you.

16:31.130 --> 16:34.110
That's right! Let's have kimchi stew for today's menu.

16:34.270 --> 16:34.760
<i>Huh?</i>

16:36.060 --> 16:38.870
I haven't heard the words "I love you" from you.

16:39.260 --> 16:41.260
Wha? I <i>did</i> say it!

16:41.560 --> 16:46.050
Your "I love you" is always preceded by "I think" or followed by "probably".

16:46.640 --> 16:47.270
<i>Huh?</i>

16:48.000 --> 16:51.650
<i>Could it be... it's because I never said that I love Usagi-san?</i>

16:52.900 --> 16:55.600
<i>It's not like I need to say it every single time.</i>

16:56.430 --> 16:59.470
No matter how strongly you feel in your heart,

16:59.800 --> 17:03.260
if you don't convey it to the other person, it's meaningless.

17:04.340 --> 17:06.500
It's because a certain someone won't be clear on it.

17:07.320 --> 17:11.070
<i>Is Usagi-san nervous... because I never responded properly?</i>

17:12.160 --> 17:15.950
<i>To begin with... how do I even feel exactly?</i>

17:16.920 --> 17:19.580
<i>If Usagi-san hooked up with someone else...</i>

17:20.000 --> 17:21.560
<i>N-No, that would be bad.</i>

17:22.170 --> 17:23.470
<i>If someone snatched him away...</i>

17:24.440 --> 17:25.820
<i>No, that won't be good either.</i>

17:26.840 --> 17:28.840
<i>Getting these nervous feelings means,</i>

17:29.650 --> 17:32.150
<i>I-It's love, is it?</i>

17:33.050 --> 17:34.480
I'm going to take a bath first.

17:36.220 --> 17:37.290
Usagi-san!

17:37.360 --> 17:39.150
I... lo-...

17:42.420 --> 17:44.530
Ahh..., no, nothing!

17:47.420 --> 17:48.450
<i>That's not good!</i>

17:48.640 --> 17:50.750
<i>At this rate, it's the same as always!</i>

17:51.170 --> 17:54.540
Just give it to him! Like a real man, to the point, wham, thud!

17:56.440 --> 17:57.070
No...

17:57.810 --> 18:00.200
I mean... I...

18:11.580 --> 18:15.670
I'm sorry!! I'm at my limit!!

18:16.960 --> 18:19.600
<i>This is bad. I suck too much at this.</i>

18:26.820 --> 18:29.770
Why you! Taking advantage of the moment...!

18:32.780 --> 18:33.650
Thank you.

18:34.280 --> 18:35.200
I'm happy.

18:35.440 --> 18:35.960
<i>Huh?</i>

18:36.660 --> 18:37.890
<i>It's his usual face.</i>

18:39.690 --> 18:41.800
U-Um... I...

18:44.210 --> 18:45.490
If you say so,

18:46.210 --> 18:47.910
I get your feelings loud and clear.

18:47.910 --> 18:50.350
Hey! Put me down! Put me down!

18:50.530 --> 18:53.280
And besides, I haven't even said anything yet!

18:53.280 --> 18:56.460
That's enough. Even if things aren't said aloud they can still be felt.

18:56.530 --> 18:58.840
You too haven't said anything!

18:59.180 --> 19:01.920
In that case, you say it first.

19:09.180 --> 19:09.970
Eh?

19:10.440 --> 19:11.530
Oh, it's alright.

19:12.080 --> 19:14.620
That's not good! It's bleeding again!

19:15.080 --> 19:16.770
I'll rewrap it. Give me your hand.

19:20.350 --> 19:21.100
Lick it.

19:23.810 --> 19:24.890
<i>I'd really regret it,</i>

19:25.200 --> 19:26.520
<i>if he found out,</i>

19:27.200 --> 19:31.720
<i>how hard my heart is beating, all because of stupid old Usagi.</i>

19:35.810 --> 19:36.690
Misaki.

19:36.960 --> 19:37.900
Look at me.

19:42.200 --> 19:43.050
I love you.

19:44.630 --> 19:46.930
<i>Don't whisper in that voice.</i>

19:47.720 --> 19:51.030
<i>Don't look at me... from this close.</i>

20:01.150 --> 20:02.050
I love you.

20:02.680 --> 20:04.030
Shut up.

20:04.190 --> 20:07.380
Even if you say the same thing over and over, doesn't mean everything's okay.

20:07.730 --> 20:08.930
That's not true.

20:11.800 --> 20:13.870
The more you say it, the deeper it goes.

20:16.030 --> 20:18.170
<i>What pisses me off about him is,</i>

20:18.380 --> 20:22.070
<i>how he acts all calm and composed like that,</i>

20:22.620 --> 20:25.240
<i>as if he's seeing right into my heart.</i>

20:27.160 --> 20:28.080
I love you.

20:31.470 --> 20:34.110
<i>Seriously... he pisses me off.</i>

20:45.720 --> 20:50.860
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

20:45.720 --> 20:50.860
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

20:50.990 --> 20:56.250
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

20:50.990 --> 20:56.250
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

20:56.600 --> 21:01.620
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

20:56.600 --> 21:01.620
You doubled all my happiness,

21:01.620 --> 21:08.310
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

21:01.620 --> 21:08.310
and halved all my sadness.

21:08.420 --> 21:13.420
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

21:08.420 --> 21:13.420
No matter what path I walk in the future,

21:13.820 --> 21:18.100
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

21:13.820 --> 21:18.100
will surely lead to you.

21:18.100 --> 21:20.860
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

21:18.100 --> 21:20.860
You're there up ahead of me,

21:20.860 --> 21:23.720
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

21:20.860 --> 21:23.720
I'm there ahead of you,

21:23.720 --> 21:28.990
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

21:23.720 --> 21:28.990
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

21:28.990 --> 21:34.890
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

21:28.990 --> 21:34.890
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

21:35.480 --> 21:39.960
mou doko he mo ikanaide

21:35.480 --> 21:39.960
Hey, don't go anywhere.

21:39.960 --> 21:45.420
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

21:39.960 --> 21:45.420
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

21:45.420 --> 21:50.810
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

21:45.420 --> 21:50.810
It's casting a light at my feet.

21:50.810 --> 21:56.630
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

21:50.810 --> 21:56.630
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

21:57.020 --> 22:02.310
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

21:57.020 --> 22:02.310
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

22:07.300 --> 22:11.410
Argh!! I <i>told</i> you, the heat resistant glasses are over here!

22:11.800 --> 22:13.900
I'll write it with a damn marker for you!

22:14.040 --> 22:14.860
Oh?

22:16.400 --> 22:18.180
Hot things

22:25.280 --> 22:26.730
A-Ah, um...

22:27.000 --> 22:27.920
What is it?

22:28.540 --> 22:37.040
That is... If I'm causing you any trouble... I was thinking if I should start living on my own... and such...

22:37.770 --> 22:38.840
What's this?

22:39.530 --> 22:41.370
Who ever told you to do that?

22:41.790 --> 22:43.120
<i>You</i>, you bastard!

22:43.770 --> 22:48.330
Damn it! Do you have any idea how worried I was!?

22:53.030 --> 22:56.520
So? What happened to the rest of yesterday's confession?

22:58.350 --> 23:01.410
Although it is a mystery whether or not you have the guts.

23:01.680 --> 23:03.040
What was that!?

23:03.560 --> 23:05.330
If I <i>felt</i> like it, I could!

23:05.550 --> 23:07.700
Oh? What could you do?

23:08.040 --> 23:10.410
S-similar to all the erotic things you do!

23:17.800 --> 23:19.640
How's that? Indirect kiss!

23:20.000 --> 23:20.970
It's erotic, isn't it!?

23:24.460 --> 23:26.420
That's right. It sure is erotic.

23:26.580 --> 23:28.160
Well done.

23:29.690 --> 23:34.310
Nii-chan... as always, stupid Usagi has me wrapped up around his little finger.

23:35.500 --> 23:44.970
Raws: BDRIP (from nyaa.se)
Translation: aarinfantasy
Timing, Typesetting, Minor script editing and Encoding: asckj1

23:56.990 --> 23:59.990
Love does not follow logic
